// stdlib/xml/dsig_vectors.test.bit: signed documents and keys for dsig.test.bit.
//
// Every document was signed by libxmlsec 1.3.11 (`xmlsec1 --sign`, OpenSSL
// backend, Alpine 3.24.2 container) from a template with exclusive C14N, an
// enveloped-signature transform and a SHA-256 digest, and each was checked
// back with `xmlsec1 --verify` before it was pasted here: an implementation
// other than this one produced the signatures. Keys were made with OpenSSL
// 3.5.9 (`genrsa 2048`, `ecparam -name prime256v1`); only public halves are
// here. The signed text is exactly what xmlsec1 wrote, minus its `<?xml ...?>`
// line (the Writer never writes one). `Inc` documents name `xs saml` in an
// InclusiveNamespaces PrefixList on both the CanonicalizationMethod and the
// transform. `Resp` documents sign the Response, `Assert` documents sign the
// Assertion inside an unsigned Response.

